    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιζάφελος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>vehement, violent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.525
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λῶς</span> (as if from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιζαφελής</span>, which never occurs,
				v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				769.22
			</span></i>) <i>vehe mently</i>,<i>furiously</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. χαλεπαίνειν, μενεαίνειν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.516
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.330
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεείνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					487
				</span></i>
			: also neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιζάφελον κοτέουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1672
				</span></i>
			.</div>
